 "sq": [
  {
   "_id": 5219,
   "ANSWER": "<p style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">In a Binary Search Tree (BST), each node stores a value and has pointers to its left and right child nodes. When implemented using a linked list approach, each node is dynamically created and connected using pointers, enabling flexibility in memory management.</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>Structure of a Node in BST using Linked List</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">struct Node {</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; int data;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; // Stores the value</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; struct Node* left;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; // Pointer to the left child</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; struct Node* right;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; // Pointer to the right child</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">};</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">This structure uses <b>self-referencing pointers</b>, meaning each node contains pointers that reference other nodes of the same type.</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>How its Supports Dynamic Memory Allocation:</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<ol>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>Memory is Allocated Only When Needed:</b></span></span></span></span>\n\n\t<ul style=\"list-style-type:circle\">\n\t\t<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 72.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Using malloc() in C (or new in C++), we allocate memory for each node at runtime.</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t\t<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 72.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">There&#39;s <b>no need to define the tree size beforehand</b>, unlike arrays.</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>Efficient Insertion &amp; Deletion:</b></span></span></span></span>\n\t<ul style=\"list-style-type:circle\">\n\t\t<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 72.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Nodes can be added or removed without shifting elements (as would be needed in an array).</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t\t<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 72.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Left and right child pointers can be easily updated to maintain BST properties.</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>Non-contiguous Memory Storage:</b></span></span></span></span>\n\t<ul style=\"list-style-type:circle\">\n\t\t<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 72.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Nodes are stored in <b>non-contiguous locations</b> in memory, but logically linked through pointers.</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t\t<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 72.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">This allows better usage of available memory and avoids fragmentation issues.</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>Flexible Tree Growth:</b></span></span></span></span>\n\t<ul style=\"list-style-type:circle\">\n\t\t<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 72.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Trees can grow in depth or width as needed, constrained only by system memory.</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t\t<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 72.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">There is <b>no fixed size limit</b> for the number of nodes.</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>Supports Recursive Operations:</b></span></span></span></span>\n\t<ul style=\"list-style-type:circle\">\n\t\t<li style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 72.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Since each node points to its children, operations like <b>search, insert, delete, traversals</b> can be easily implemented using recursion.</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n</ol>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\">&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>Example of Node Creation:</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">struct Node* createNode(int key) {</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; struct Node* newNode = (struct Node*)malloc(sizeof(struct Node));</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; newNode-&gt;data = key;</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; newNode-&gt;left = NULL;</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; newNode-&gt;right = NULL;</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; return newNode;</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">}</span></span></span></p>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSC201J",
   "LEVEL": 2,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO1",
    "PLO13",
    "PLO3",
    "PLO2",
    "PLO12"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p style=\"margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>Describe the structure of a node in a Binary Search Tree (BST) when implemented using a linked list. How does this structure facilitate dynamic memory allocation and efficient tree operations?</b></span></span></span></p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 409,
   "TYPE": "sq",
   "key": 5219
  },
  {
   "_id": 5220,
   "ANSWER": "<p style=\"margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>1. Dynamic Memory Allocation</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Linked List BST uses dynamic memory allocation, meaning memory is allocated at runtime as new nodes are created.</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Array BST typically requires pre-allocating a fixed amount of memory, which can lead to either wasted space or memory shortage.</span></span></span></span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>2. No Wasted Memory</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">In linked list BST, each node occupies memory only when required.</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">In an array, unused indices still occupy space.</span></span></span></span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>3. Efficient Insertion and Deletion</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">In a linked list BST, inserting or deleting a node involves simple pointer changes without shifting elements.</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">In an array, insertion/deletion often requires shifting elements or restructuring the array.</span></span></span></span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>4. No Fixed Size Limitation</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Arrays have a fixed size unless a dynamic array (like vector in C++) is used.</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Linked list BST grows as needed without reallocation.</span></span></span></span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>5. Better Representation of Tree Structure</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">In linked list, each node contains a pointer to its left and right child, making it more natural and intuitive to represent a tree.</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">In array representation, maintaining parent-child relationships requires index calculations:</span></span></span></span>\n\t<ul style=\"list-style-type:circle\">\n\t\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 72.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Left child: 2 * i + 1</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 72.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Right child: 2 * i + 2</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>6. Easier Implementation of Recursive Operations</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Recursive tree traversals like In-order, Pre-order, and Post-order are more straightforward in linked list implementation due to node references.</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Array representation often complicates these with index tracking.</span></span></span></span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>7. Adaptability to Balanced Trees</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Advanced self-balancing BSTs (like AVL or Red-Black Trees) are efficiently implemented using linked list structures due to flexible node manipulation.</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"text-align:justify; margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">In arrays, rebalancing would involve complex resizing and shifting.</span></span></span></span></li>\n</ul>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSC201J",
   "LEVEL": 2,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO1",
    "PLO13",
    "PLO3",
    "PLO2",
    "PLO12"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p style=\"margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>Discuss the advantages of implementing a Binary Search Tree (BST) using a linked list compared to using an array.</b></span></span></span></p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 409,
   "TYPE": "sq",
   "key": 5220
  }
 ],
 "lq": [
  {
   "_id": 5239,
   "ANSWER": "<p style=\"margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>Node Structure for BST Using Linked List in C</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">#include &lt;stdlib.h&gt;</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">struct Node {</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; int data;</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; struct Node* left;</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; struct Node* right;</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">};</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Each node contains:</span></span></span></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li style=\"margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">data: the student ID</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">left: pointer to the left subtree</span></span></span></span></li>\n\t<li style=\"margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"tab-stops:list 36.0pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">right: pointer to the right subtree</span></span></span></span></li>\n</ul>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:107%\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>Create a New Node</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">struct Node* createNode(int data) {</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; struct Node* newNode = (struct Node*)malloc(sizeof(struct Node));</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; newNode-&gt;data = data;</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; newNode-&gt;left = newNode-&gt;right = NULL;</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; return newNode;</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">}</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><strong><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Insertion Operation</span></span></span></strong></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">struct Node* insert(struct Node* root, int data) {</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; if (root == NULL)</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; return createNode(data);</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; if (data &lt; root-&gt;data)</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; root-&gt;left = insert(root-&gt;left, data);</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; else if (data &gt; root-&gt;data)</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; root-&gt;right = insert(root-&gt;right, data);</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; return root;</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">}</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>Search Operation</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">struct Node* search(struct Node* root, int key) {</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; if (root == NULL || root-&gt;data == key)</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; return root;</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; if (key &lt; root-&gt;data)</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; return search(root-&gt;left, key);</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; else</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; return search(root-&gt;right, key);</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">}</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>Find Minimum Value Node (Used in Deletion)</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">struct Node* findMin(struct Node* root) {</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; while (root-&gt;left != NULL)</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; root = root-&gt;left;</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; return root;</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">}</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>Deletion Operation</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">struct Node* deleteNode(struct Node* root, int key) {</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; if (root == NULL) return root;</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; if (key &lt; root-&gt;data)</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; root-&gt;left = deleteNode(root-&gt;left, key);</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; else if (key &gt; root-&gt;data)</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; root-&gt;right = deleteNode(root-&gt;right, key);</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; else {</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; // Node with one child or no child</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; if (root-&gt;left == NULL) {</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; struct Node* temp = root-&gt;right;</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; free(root);</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; return temp;</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; } else if (root-&gt;right == NULL) {</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; struct Node* temp = root-&gt;left;</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; free(root);</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; return temp;</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; }</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; // Node with two children: Get inorder successor (min in right subtree)</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; struct Node* temp = findMin(root-&gt;right);</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; root-&gt;data = temp-&gt;data;</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; root-&gt;right = deleteNode(root-&gt;right, temp-&gt;data);</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; }</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; return root;</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">}</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>In-Order Traversal</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">void inOrder(struct Node* root) {</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; if (root != NULL) {</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; inOrder(root-&gt;left);</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; printf(&quot;%d &quot;, root-&gt;data);</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; inOrder(root-&gt;right);</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; }</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">}</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>Main Function to Test</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">int main() {</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; struct Node* root = NULL;</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; // Insertion</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; int ids[] = {101, 85, 120, 70, 90, 110, 130};</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; for (int i = 0; i &lt; 7; i++)</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; root = insert(root, ids[i]);</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; printf(&quot;In-order Traversal after Insertion:\\n&quot;);</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; inOrder(root);&nbsp; // Output: 70 85 90 101 110 120 130</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; printf(&quot;\\n&quot;);</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; // Search</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; int searchID = 90;</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; struct Node* found = search(root, searchID);</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; if (found != NULL)</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; printf(&quot;Student ID %d found in the system.\\n&quot;, searchID);</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; else</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; printf(&quot;Student ID %d not found.\\n&quot;, searchID);</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; // Deletion</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; root = deleteNode(root, 85);</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; printf(&quot;In-order Traversal after Deletion of 85:\\n&quot;);</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; inOrder(root);&nbsp; // Output: 70 90 101 110 120 130</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; printf(&quot;\\n&quot;);</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; return 0;</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">}</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\"><b>Output:</b></span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">In-order Traversal after Insertion:</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">70 85 90 101 110 120 130</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">Student ID 90 found in the system.</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">In-order Traversal after Deletion of 85:</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"line-height:normal\"><span style=\"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif\">70 90 101 110 120 130</span></span></span></p>\n\n<p style=\"margin-bottom:11px\">&nbsp;</p>\n",
